//
// Gate E cell: a range walked by a comprehension or by a `for` in a format hole.  The element is
// the walk's own type (a `u8` start inside its width types the vector `vector<u8>`); the format
// hole's `{id}#index` is made first at the count type (`iter_for`), and a range with more than
// one init step (a computed bound: its `_range_start_N`, the null guard, `_next_N`) keeps that
// `create_iter` as an `Insert` of its own inside the loop's (`iter_init_steps`).
// Prints: [250,251,252,253,254,255] [251,252,253] [3,4,5,6] [1,2] [250,251,252] [3,4,5]

fn main() {
  a: u8 = 250;
  b = 3;
  v = [for x in a..=255 { x }];
  w = [for x in a..253 { x + 1 }];
  println("{v} {w} {for x in b..7 { x }} {for x in 1..b { x }} {for x in a..=252 { x }} {for x in b.. { if x > 5 { break; } x }}");
}
